    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` pipeline already emitted an `AUDIT` log on successful create ([`AuditOwnerCreated`](src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java)). I added a parallel welcome-notification step following the same OfficeFloor pattern:\n\n1. **New function** `EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java` \u2014 reads the saved `@Val Owner` and emits a single line on the logger named `NOTIFY` containing both the owner id and the `memberId`:\n   ```\n   NOTIFY - Welcome notification enqueued: id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1\n   ```\n\n2. **Wired it into** `owners.POST.yml` as a `welcome:` step between `audit` and `respond`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like the surrounding steps. It runs after `SaveOwner`, so the generated `id` and `memberId` are both populated.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts the line carries both the owner id and memberId \u2014 it passes.",
